! GaAs with spin-orbit coupling in an external magnetic field: the ground state
! the magnetoelectric tensor is differenced from.
!
! This is Elk's own `examples/magnetoelectric/GaAs` (task 390), and the reason
! that example exists is the physics this input is set up for. **The linear
! magnetoelectric tensor vanishes in any time-reversal-symmetric crystal**, so a
! non-magnetic semiconductor has none -- and Elk's answer is to apply a large
! external field to break time reversal by hand, then difference the
! polarization against a *small* further change in it. The magnetism is induced
! rather than spontaneous, which is what makes a plain gapped semiconductor a
! usable case at all.
!
! GaAs is zincblende, so it is **not centrosymmetric** either, which is the
! other symmetry that would force the tensor to zero. Both conditions matter and
! this cell is the cheapest crystal here that meets both: `alas-raman.in`'s twin
! with relativistic datasets, since spin-orbit coupling is what couples the spin
! the field acts on to the lattice the polarization is measured along. Without
! it the tensor vanishes identically, which is this phase's sharpest null.
!
! From Elk's file, converted: `scale 10.6826` is celldm(1), the fcc `avec` is
! ibrav = 2, `spinpol`/`spinorb` are noncolin/lspinorb, and `bfieldc 0 0 0.1` is
! B_field(3). Elk's `deltabf 0.05` is the finite-difference step and belongs to
! the workflow rather than to this file.
!
! `nosym`/`noinv` because the response is direction-dependent and the field
! lowers the symmetry anyway; the cutoffs are well below convergence and are set
! for a machine rather than for a number -- what is validated on this cell are
! the identities (the spin-orbit null and the linearity), not an absolute.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.6826, nat = 2, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 22.0, ecutrho = 176.0,
    noncolin = .true., lspinorb = .true.,
    nosym = .true., noinv = .true.,
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.01, angle1(1) = 0.0,
    starting_magnetization(2) = 0.01, angle1(2) = 0.0,
    B_field(3) = 0.1
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-9
    mixing_beta = 0.3
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Ga 69.723 Ga.rel-pbe-dn-rrkjus_psl.1.0.0.UPF
 As 74.922 As.rel-pbe-n-rrkjus_psl.1.0.0.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 Ga 0.00 0.00 0.00
 As 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 2 2 2 0 0 0
